331
00:19:31.519 --> 00:19:41.781
Load shedding (a concurrency limit with a fast 503) saves the service (Ch 18), but the winners are whoever's retry lands at the right moment.

332
00:19:43.131 --> 00:19:48.933
A waiting room hands out tickets in arrival order and admits them at a rate the backend can sustain.

333
00:19:49.213 --> 00:19:54.824
The database sees a steady load, every customer has a position, and first come is first served.

334
00:19:55.104 --> 00:20:05.131
Real waiting rooms add a pre-queue before the sale starts (randomised order among early arrivals), per-customer limits, and bot protection (Ch 39).

335
00:20:05.411 --> 00:20:11.064
Idempotent checkout: a customer's retry must return their existing order, not sold out.

336
00:20:12.414 --> 00:20:14.846
