394
00:24:19.821 --> 00:24:22.573
Payments, Dark-store ops, Marketing, SRE.

395
00:24:22.853 --> 00:24:38.810
Context, Diwali flash sale: one hot row saturated the pool; timeouts and retries amplified load; 30-minute holds stranded stock; late payments charged for sold-out items; phantom stock caused missing items; outcomes were unfair.

396
00:24:40.160 --> 00:25:01.621
Decision, Atomic conditional updates with stock buckets for hot SKUs and a Redis gate for flash sales; reservation leases with short TTL extended on payment start and an explicit late-capture path; per-SKU buffers learned from picking plus immediate corrections; waiting room with FIFO admission for flash sales; idempotent checkout.

397
00:25:02.971 --> 00:25:16.646
Related ADRs, ADR-320 Reservation = one small transaction: conditional UPDATE + INSERT; no remote calls inside (L1); ADR-321 Hot SKUs:

398
00:25:16.926 --> 00:25:30.302
16 buckets, sold-out flag, Redis gate seeded from DB and reconciled every minute (L1); ADR-322 TTL 3 min, extend to 15 min on payment start; late capture,

399
00:25:30.582 --> 00:25:57.014
then re-reserve or auto-refund (L2); ADR-323 Per-SKU buffers from 7-day pick failures; picker missing corrects stock and opens a cycle count (L3); ADR-324 Flash sales behind a waiting room admitting at 70% of measured checkout capacity, FIFO with randomised pre-queue (L4); ADR-325 Checkout idempotency key returns the original outcome.

400
00:25:57.294 --> 00:25:58.254
Requirements.

401
00:25:59.604 --> 00:26:05.684
R1 Zero oversell against recorded stock; missing-item orders 0.5%.

402
00:26:05.964 --> 00:26:10.487
R2 Flash sales never degrade checkout for other items (bulkheads).

403
00:26:10.767 --> 00:26:19.279
R3 Every customer in a flash sale gets an answer within 30 s; buyers ≥ 90% in arrival order.

404
00:26:19.559 --> 00:26:23.569
R4 Late captures refunded automatically within 5 minutes.

405
00:26:23.849 --> 00:26:30.164
R5 Stranded stock (held by abandoned checkouts) 5% of flash-sale stock at any time.

406
00:26:30.444 --> 00:26:31.852
Decisions in detail.

407
00:26:33.202 --> 00:26:47.197
Stock model (ADR-320 or 321). stock(store, sku, bucket, qty CHECK qty = 0); buckets = 1 normally, 16 for configured hot SKUs.

408
00:26:47.477 --> 00:26:50.058
Leases (ADR-322).

409
00:26:50.338 --> 00:26:56.034
Reservation rows with expiresat; sweeper every 10 s; payment-started events extend.

410
00:26:56.314 --> 00:26:58.938
Accuracy (ADR-323).

411
00:26:59.218 --> 00:27:06.237
Buffer = ceil(1.5 times daily average misses) per SKU per store; nightly recompute.

412
00:27:06.517 --> 00:27:09.375
Waiting room (ADR-324).

413
00:27:09.655 --> 00:27:14.797
Edge-hosted queue; tokens signed; admission rate adjusted from checkout latency.

414
00:27:16.147 --> 00:27:19.197
Idempotency (ADR-325).

415
00:27:19.477 --> 00:27:22.955
Keys stored with outcome for 24 h (Ch 20).

416
00:27:23.235 --> 00:27:24.259
Consequences.

417
00:27:24.539 --> 00:27:34.160
More moving parts for flash sales (gate, buckets, waiting room); buffers hide some sellable stock; short TTLs require the late-capture path.

418
00:27:34.440 --> 00:27:42.440
In return: sales that finish in seconds without collateral damage, fewer missing items, and outcomes customers can see are fair.

